  "notes": "A 90° off-axis parabolic mirror (parent focal length 25.4 mm, so a reflected focal length of 50.8 mm) focuses a collimated beam to a point with no spherical aberration and no chromatic aberration, and folds it out of the way. Compare it with a spherical mirror: set the conic k to 0 and look at the spot and wavefront error on the screen. The ray fan shows the aberration directly."
